12. Advantages
Very easy state machine.
Excellent for learning thread alternation.
Demonstrates wait/notify clearly.
No mathematical conditions.
13. Disadvantages
Only models two-thread coordination.
Doesn't scale naturally to many threads.
14. Common Mistakes

❌ Using if instead of while.

❌ Forgetting notifyAll().

❌ Initializing the turn incorrectly.

❌ Calling sleep() instead of wait().

❌ Busy waiting.

15. Best Practices
One shared object.
One boolean state.
One monitor.
Always use while.
Prefer restoring interrupt status when interrupted.
16. Interview Questions
Q1

Why is one boolean enough?

Because there are only two execution states:

Foo
Bar
Q2

Can we use an enum?

Yes.

But for only two states,

a boolean is simpler.

Q3

Why not use sleep()?

Because sleep() doesn't release the monitor.

Q4

Why notifyAll()?

It is the safer general pattern. Although notify() would usually work with exactly two threads, interviewers generally prefer notifyAll() because it scales better to future changes.

Q5

Can this be solved using Semaphore?

Yes.

