Notice something:

Problem	State Representation
Odd–Even	Parity (number % 2)
Producer–Consumer	Buffer state (empty/full)
Remainder	number % 3
Zero-Even-Odd	Three-state turn (ZERO, ODD, EVEN)
FooBar	Two-state turn (FOO, BAR)

You're now seeing the same underlying synchronization pattern expressed through different state representations.